## 解答

**问题.** 对于非负整数 $m \geq 1$，计算
$$1 - \int_0^1 \left\{\frac{1}{x}\right\}^m x^m\,dx.$$

### 第一步：在区间上展开

对于 $x \in (0,1]$，有 $1/x \geq 1$。在区间 $x \in \bigl(\frac{1}{n+1},\, \frac{1}{n}\bigr]$（$n=1,2,\dots$）上，$\frac{1}{x} \in [n, n+1)$，故 $\lfloor 1/x \rfloor = n$，从而
$$\left\{\frac{1}{x}\right\} = \frac{1}{x} - n, \qquad \left\{\frac{1}{x}\right\}^m x^m = (1 - nx)^m.$$

因此
$$\int_0^1 \left\{\frac{1}{x}\right\}^m x^m\,dx = \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \int_{1/(n+1)}^{1/n} (1-nx)^m\,dx.$$

### 第二步：换元计算每个积分

在每项中令 $u = nx$，$du = n\,dx$；当 $x = \frac{1}{n+1}$ 时 $u = \frac{n}{n+1}$，当 $x = \frac{1}{n}$ 时 $u = 1$。再令 $t = 1-u$：
$$\int_{1/(n+1)}^{1/n} (1-nx)^m\,dx = \frac{1}{n}\int_{n/(n+1)}^{1}(1-u)^m\,du = \frac{1}{n}\int_0^{1/(n+1)} t^m\,dt = \frac{1}{n(m+1)(n+1)^{m+1}}.$$

于是
$$\int_0^1 \left\{\frac{1}{x}\right\}^m x^m\,dx = \frac{1}{m+1}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{n\,(n+1)^{m+1}}.$$

### 第三步：部分分式分解

**断言.**
$$\frac{1}{n(n+1)^{m+1}} = \frac{1}{n} - \sum_{k=1}^{m+1}\frac{1}{(n+1)^k}.$$

*证明.* 两边乘以 $n(n+1)^{m+1}$，令 $u = n+1$，需证
$$1 = u^{m+1} - (u-1)\sum_{k=1}^{m+1}u^{m+1-k}.$$
而 $\sum_{k=1}^{m+1}u^{m+1-k} = u^m + u^{m-1}+\cdots+1 = \frac{u^{m+1}-1}{u-1}$，故右边 $= u^{m+1} - (u^{m+1}-1) = 1$。$\square$

### 第四步：求和

将分解式代入并分离 $k=1$ 的发散部分（与 $\frac1n$ 抵消）：
$$\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{n(n+1)^{m+1}} = \underbrace{\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\left(\frac{1}{n}-\frac{1}{n+1}\right)}_{=1\text{（望远镜）}} - \sum_{k=2}^{m+1}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(n+1)^k}.$$

对 $k\ge 2$，$\displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(n+1)^k} = \sum_{j=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{j^k} = \zeta(k)-1$。因此
$$\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{n(n+1)^{m+1}} = 1 - \sum_{k=2}^{m+1}\bigl(\zeta(k)-1\bigr) = 1 - \sum_{k=2}^{m+1}\zeta(k) + m = (m+1) - \sum_{k=2}^{m+1}\zeta(k).$$

### 第五步：最终结果

$$\int_0^1 \left\{\frac{1}{x}\right\}^m x^m\,dx = \frac{1}{m+1}\left[(m+1) - \sum_{k=2}^{m+1}\zeta(k)\right] = 1 - \frac{1}{m+1}\sum_{k=2}^{m+1}\zeta(k).$$

故
$$\boxed{\,1 - \int_0^1 \left\{\frac{1}{x}\right\}^m x^m\,dx \;=\; \frac{1}{m+1}\sum_{k=2}^{m+1}\zeta(k)\,}.$$

### 验证

- **$m=1$：** $\frac{1}{2}\zeta(2) = \frac{\pi^2}{12}$。直接计算 $\int_0^1\{1/x\}\,x\,dx = 1 - \frac{\zeta(2)}{2}$，故 $1 - \text{积分} = \frac{\zeta(2)}{2}$。✓
- **$m=2$：** $\frac{1}{3}\bigl(\zeta(2)+\zeta(3)\bigr)$，与逐项积分一致。✓

